# A copy of Extrapolate the Impossible is a copy of the whole spell (CR 707.10): the copy resolves first, its controller
# (Bot1, who controls the copy, CR 707.10a) reveals two cards of their own from outside the game again, and the card Bot2
# names is brought into Bot1's hand - so the original, resolving afterwards, chooses from a sideboard the copy has already
# taken one card out of. Bot1's three Moxen and Black Lotus pay for both spells on the first turn.

[Bot1 Deck]
Extrapolate the Impossible
Lutri, the Spellchaser
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
Island
Island
Island x13

[Bot1 Sideboard]
Lightning Bolt
Counterspell
Duress

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Extrapolate the Impossible.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Lutri, the Spellchaser.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Choose(Counterspell)
Bot2.Choose(Counterspell)
Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Choose(Duress)
Bot2.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
[T1 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Counterspell; Island; Island; Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Sideboard = Duress
Bot1.Graveyard = Extrapolate the Impossible; Black Lotus
Stack.Count = 0
